#: of pysme.atmosphere.interpolation.AtmosphereInterpolator.interp_atmo_pair:1
msgid ""
"Interpolate between two model atmospheres, accounting for shifts in the "
"mass column density or optical depth scale."
msgstr ""

#: of pysme.atmosphere.interpolation.AtmosphereInterpolator.interp_atmo_pair:4
msgid "How it works:"
msgstr ""

#: of pysme.atmosphere.interpolation.AtmosphereInterpolator.interp_atmo_pair:6
msgid ""
"1. The second atmosphere is fitted onto the first, individually for each "
"of the four atmospheric quantitites: T, xne, xna, rho. The fitting uses a"
" linear shift in both the (log) depth parameter and in the (log) "
"atmospheric quantity. For T, the midpoint of the two atmospheres is "
"aligned for the initial guess. The result of this fit is used as initial "
"guess for the other quantities. A penalty function is applied to each "
"fit, to avoid excessively large shifts on the depth scale. 2. The mean of"
" the horizontal shift in each parameter is used to construct the common "
"output depth scale. 3. Each atmospheric quantity is interpolated after "
"shifting the two corner models by the amount determined in step 1), "
"rescaled by the interpolation fraction (frac)."
msgstr ""

#: of pysme.atmosphere.interpolation.AtmosphereInterpolator.interp_atmo_pair:20
msgid "first atmosphere to interpolate"
msgstr ""

#: of pysme.atmosphere.interpolation.AtmosphereInterpolator.interp_atmo_pair:22
msgid "second atmosphere to interpolate"
msgstr ""

#: of pysme.atmosphere.interpolation.AtmosphereInterpolator.interp_atmo_pair:24
msgid "interpolation fraction: 0.0 -> atmo1 and 1.0 -> atmo2"
msgstr ""

#: of pysme.atmosphere.interpolation.AtmosphereInterpolator.interp_atmo_pair:26
msgid "atmosphere interpolation variable (default:\"RHOX\")."
msgstr ""

#: of pysme.atmosphere.interpolation.AtmosphereInterpolator.interp_atmo_pair:28
msgid ""
"index of top point in the atmosphere to use. default is to use all points"
" (itop=0). use itop=1 to clip top depth point."
msgstr ""

